scornful:
He took his anodyne;
With scornful grace, he bowed farewell
And retraversed the line.

scolded:
So, smoothed and silenced you lie, like a child, not again
to be questioned or scolded;
But, for you, not one of us believes that this is rest.

scores:
We’ll liken to a brutalised King Lear,
Led out,—by no means to clear scores with wrongs—
His wrongs are so far back, ... he has forgot;

scorn:
Thou who didst bear for me the crown of thorn,
Spitting and scorn;
Though I till now have put forth thorns, yet now

scourge:
"Cease thy complaints, mine be the task assign'd
"To punish pride, and scourge the rebel mind."
This Phoebe join'd.--They wing their instant flight;

scold:
I'm as triflin' as the children,
Though I blame them lots an' scold;
I keep slippin' to the spring-house,

scooped:
I taste a liquor never brewed,
From tankards scooped in pearl;
Not all the vats upon the Rhine

scout:
And my teeth were small like pearls;
The girls might flout and scout me,
But the boys would hang about me

Lest the Bridegroom hear him;
Scout him and rout him
With his ominous eye about him.

scorpions:
Without lair or nest on either hand:
Only scorpions jerked in the sand,
Black as black iron, or dusty pale;

scows:
Are all a-quiver;
I know how many skiffs and scows
Are on the river.

scoun'el:
An' I 's comin' back to see you jes' as ehly as I kin,
So you better not go spa'kin' wif dat wuffless scoun'el Quin!
Well, I reckon, I mus' close now; write ez soon's dis reaches you;

scootin:
Wen I git up in de mo'nin' an' de clouds is big an' black,
Dey's a kin' o' wa'nin' shivah goes a-scootin' down my back;
Den I says to my ol' ooman ez I watches down de lane,

scoun'els:
I kin feel de fish a-waitin' w'en I strikes de rivah's san';
Nevah min', you ho'ny scoun'els, need n' swim erroun' an' grin,
I 'll be grinnin' in a minute w'en I 'mence to haul you in.

scoop:
Grand go the years in the crescent above them;
Worlds scoop their arcs, and firmaments row,
Diadems drop and Doges surrender,

And started all abroad;
The dust did scoop itself like hands
And throw away the road.
